     * times): slots are handed out in order(), a batch build only gets a slot while fewer than batchCap() batch builds hold
     * one (the reservation), a running build past `runMs` is assumed to need a quarter of runMs more (never zero), a build
     * waiting for an AI retry not before its retryAt, and `extraMs` (the AI breaker's hold) delays builds that need the AI.
     * Sorted by start time (ties keep order()). With no duration (runMs <= 0) a nominal one only ORDERS the line.
